{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1785007854,"nonce":"9MXvpOYhEwwq+yD6MjqDEKt1EqI=","title":"oauth: SCARAB_OAUTH_OWNERS is unusable against a real OIDC issuer","message":"Subject precedence in oauth.rs:121-127 is `sub` -\u003e `login` -\u003e `id`, and the Owner bootstrap (oauth.rs:134) matches SCARAB_OAUTH_OWNERS against that subject.\n\nWith GitHub/Forgejo the subject is a human-readable login, so the config reads fine. With a real OIDC issuer (Dex, Keycloak, Google) `sub` is an opaque per-client identifier, so bootstrapping owners means discovering and pasting opaque UUIDs before anyone can administer anything — a chicken-and-egg at first boot.\n\nFix: allow matching an owner entry against a VERIFIED email claim (email + email_verified) in addition to the subject, while keeping `sub` as the stable stored Principal identity. Unverified email must never grant Owner.","files":null}]}